&lt;p&gt;BanglaFakeCard is a corpus of 3,962 Bengali news photocards from 19 news outlets, 1,960 authentic and 2,002 fabricated. Photocards are square images carrying a headline and an outlet logo, and are a dominant format for Bengali news circulation on social media. Because the headline is rendered into the image, text-based fake news detectors cannot read it. Each image carries an EasyOCR transcription with a mean per-region confidence score, an LLM-cleaned caption, a tier label (authentic, branded fake, generic unbranded fake), an outlet code, a news genre and a collector identifier. Width, height, file size and a SHA-256 hash are published for every image.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This deposit has two access layers. The annotations, transcriptions, split definitions and metadata are open under CC BY 4.0. The photocard images are restricted and released on request, because copyright in them is held by the originating news outlets and the depositors cannot grant a public licence over that material. The restriction is a rights constraint, not a privacy one; the corpus contains no personal data. The published SHA-256 hashes let a recipient verify that the archive they were granted matches the one the published results were computed on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The corpus is confounded twice over, and the deposit documents both. Every outlet is either entirely authentic or entirely fabricated, and the two classes differ systematically in image resolution: a classifier that reads only width, height and file size, and never opens a single pixel, reaches 93.8 percent accuracy under a stratified random split. The width, height and bytes columns are published precisely so this confound stays auditable without access to the images. The recommended protocol is therefore outlet-disjoint 5-fold cross-validation in which every fold holds out a complete parody pair, so a model never sees a genuine template in training and its imitation at test time. Both split definitions ship with the deposit; the random stratified split is included only so the shortcut ceiling can be reproduced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Known limitation: per-post permalinks were not recorded at collection time, so there is no source URL column and the corpus cannot be independently rebuilt from public sources.&lt;/p&gt;
